diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 72b2a1d..7b259e4 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -81,6 +81,71 @@ Two changes worth making at the same time, now that you own the backend:
 For the brochure modal in `index.html`, same idea against
 `/api/public/brochure-requests`.
 
+## Email: Gmail + Resend
+
+Two services, split by purpose:
+
+| Email | Sent through |
+|---|---|
+| Registration confirmation, brochure email, payment reminder, seat-selection invite, internal team alerts, admin replies | **Gmail** |
+| Campaigns (bulk sends from `/admin/campaigns`) | **Resend** |
+
+Why the split: Gmail caps daily sending (about 500 recipients on a free account,
+2,000 on Google Workspace), which is plenty for one-to-one emails but not for
+blasting a whole audience; Resend is built for that and reports delivery/opens.
+Gmail is also the mailbox replies arrive in, which is what powers the **Replies**
+tab. Campaigns are sent with Reply-To set to the Gmail address, so replies to a
+campaign land in the same inbox.
+
+Things that change because of this:
+
+- Gmail-sent emails record **Sent / Failed** (and **Bounced**, detected from
+  Gmail's bounce notices) but not Delivered/Opened — Gmail doesn't report those.
+  Campaign emails still get the full Resend tracking.
+- A template's own Reply-To is not used for attendee emails; replies go to the
+  Gmail address so they can be read in the admin.
+
+### Connecting Gmail (one time)
+
+1. In Google Cloud Console create a project, enable the **Gmail API**, and create
+   an **OAuth client ID** (type: Web application; add `https://developers.google.com/oauthplayground`
+   as an authorized redirect URI).
+2. If the mailbox is a **Google Workspace** account, set the OAuth consent
+   screen's user type to **Internal** — refresh tokens then don't expire. On a
+   personal Gmail account, an app left in *Testing* mode has refresh tokens that
+   **expire after 7 days**; you'd need to publish the app instead.
+3. Open the [OAuth Playground](https://developers.google.com/oauthplayground), click the gear,
+   tick *Use your own OAuth credentials*, enter the client ID/secret, then authorize
+   these two scopes while signed in as the sending mailbox:
+   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.send` and `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.readonly`.
+   Exchange the code and copy the **refresh token**.
+4. Set `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`, `GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET`, `GMAIL_REFRESH_TOKEN` and
+   `GMAIL_SENDER` (the mailbox address) in Vercel, then redeploy.
+
+Until Gmail is connected, set `TRANSACTIONAL_EMAIL_PROVIDER=resend` to keep
+sending through Resend as before.
+
+## Replies
+
+`/admin/replies` lists conversations where a participant replied to an email,
+lets any admin read and answer them (the answer is sent from the Gmail address,
+in the same thread), and shows an unread count on the tab. New replies are pulled
+from Gmail automatically while anyone has the dashboard open (throttled to about
+once a minute), or on demand with **Check for new replies**. Only mail from
+registrants and brochure requesters is imported — the rest of the mailbox is ignored.
+
+WhatsApp is not connected. The inbox is built channel-agnostic (`InboxMessage.channel`),
+so adding WhatsApp later means receiving Meta's webhook into that table and sending
+through the WhatsApp Cloud API; see the note at the top of `src/lib/inbox.ts`.
+
+## Audit log
+
+`/admin/audit` (owners only) records who did what and when: sign-ins (including
+failed attempts), payment updates and resets, every email sent or blocked,
+check-ins, deletions, exports, campaigns, replies, seat changes, template and
+settings edits, and admin changes. Entries are append-only — no page or API edits
+or deletes them, and clearing test data doesn't touch them.
+
 ## Deploying
 
 1. Push this repo, connect it to **Vercel**.
